<title>USA: SPC raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</title>
<headline>SPC raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scurlock Permian, a unit of Ashland Inc, said it had raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Thursday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $19.00 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $19.00 and Oklahoma sweet is $19.00.</p>
<p>--((New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623))</p>
</text>
